1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,720
In Module 4, we execute the Discovery Call.

2
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:11,000
When the Teams meeting begins, the Fathom bot automatically joins to record and transcribe the session.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,588
The sales team navigates to the Session tab to view the qualification battlecard.

4
00:00:16,588 --> 00:00:25,558
In cases where the recording bot fails to connect -- due to waiting room settings or IT restrictions -- the team has backups.

5
00:00:25,558 --> 00:00:31,970
They can use the platform's built-in recording, or tools like three C X for phone-based calls.

6
00:00:31,970 --> 00:00:38,823
After the call, the representative uploads the recording directly via the Upload Recording button.

7
00:00:38,823 --> 00:00:47,882
The system accepts MP3, MP4, M4A, and WAV files and automatically transcribes the audio.

8
00:00:47,882 --> 00:00:54,220
The sales team references Playbook Variant A or B depending on the prospect's experience.

9
00:00:54,220 --> 00:01:00,382
They ask these questions conversationally, letting the recording tool capture the responses.

10
00:01:00,382 --> 00:01:08,088
Before ending the call, the sales team secures the next step by booking a Positional Meeting with the directors.

11
00:01:08,088 --> 00:01:15,588
The sales team documents their gut feel on the deal, capturing the unspoken signals and lead temperature.

12
00:01:15,588 --> 00:01:29,705
The A I validates this assessment against the transcript, classifying the lead as Hot with an eight-out-of-ten confidence score, and identifying their position in the sales funnel as a Sales Qualified Lead.

13
00:01:29,705 --> 00:01:39,882
Based on the classification, the system recommends the appropriate follow-up -- in this case, an immediate positional meeting with the technical director.

